1
00:00:00,033 --> 00:00:01,343
(Previously on...)
What's wrong with Serizawa?

2
00:00:01,367 --> 00:00:02,200
I heard he has a fever.

3
00:00:02,300 --> 00:00:03,380
I really want to see you...

4
00:00:03,467 --> 00:00:04,867
Suzuki.

5
00:00:04,967 --> 00:00:06,300
You actually came.

6
00:00:06,967 --> 00:00:08,207
Just hypothetically speaking...

7
00:00:08,233 --> 00:00:10,633
When you're hanging out with Serizawa,

8
00:00:10,733 --> 00:00:12,200
doesn't your heart ever skip a beat?

9
00:00:13,800 --> 00:00:14,967
Ah, but...

10
00:00:15,667 --> 00:00:18,167
Could it be that I...

11
00:00:18,467 --> 00:00:19,933
I should probably head...

12
00:00:20,133 --> 00:00:21,167
Don't go back yet.

13
00:00:23,733 --> 00:00:28,500
Do I like... Serizawa?

14
00:01:16,600 --> 00:01:18,300
Wait a minute, Serizawa.

15
00:01:21,467 --> 00:01:23,400
W-Wait a second!

16
00:01:44,400 --> 00:01:47,133
Can I kiss you?

17
00:01:47,867 --> 00:01:49,500
Wh-What are you talking about?

18
00:01:50,733 --> 00:01:52,300
Suzuki, you...

19
00:01:53,667 --> 00:01:56,567
You like me, don't you?

20
00:02:03,800 --> 00:02:04,800
Eh...

21
00:02:04,900 --> 00:02:05,600
Wait...

22
00:02:05,700 --> 00:02:08,467
N-No way.

23
00:02:12,433 --> 00:02:14,967
It was a dream...

24
00:02:18,500 --> 00:02:19,700
You've got to be kidding me...

25
00:02:19,800 --> 00:02:21,600
This is the worst.

26
00:02:21,700 --> 00:02:24,533
It's all because of my
overactive imagination.

27
00:02:27,133 --> 00:02:28,933
Last night,

28
00:02:31,200 --> 00:02:33,200
when I was with Serizawa,

29
00:02:33,300 --> 00:02:35,300
my heart was racing the whole time.

30
00:02:42,833 --> 00:02:44,133
I'm sorry, Serizawa.

31
00:02:44,633 --> 00:02:45,833
I think I'd better go home.

32
00:02:45,933 --> 00:02:46,933
Huh?

33
00:02:46,967 --> 00:02:48,133
I'm really sorry.

34
00:02:48,233 --> 00:02:50,500
Call me right away if you need anything.

35
00:02:50,900 --> 00:02:52,367
Get some rest.

36
00:02:57,467 --> 00:03:04,500
I really have fallen
for Serizawa, haven't I?

37
00:03:09,167 --> 00:03:10,967
(You have a new message
from Serizawa Haruto)

38
00:03:12,400 --> 00:03:13,933
Morning, Suzuki.

39
00:03:14,033 --> 00:03:15,367
Thanks for yesterday.

40
00:03:15,467 --> 00:03:17,933
Thanks to you, I'm feeling much better.

41
00:03:23,100 --> 00:03:27,267
Also, sleeping while
hugging you felt amazing.

42
00:03:28,700 --> 00:03:29,900
What?

43
00:03:31,367 --> 00:03:34,233
No... That doesn't count.

44
00:03:34,333 --> 00:03:38,200
I'm not going to fall for Serizawa.

45
00:04:24,467 --> 00:04:27,333
"Popular Serizawa Acts Weird Around Me"

46
00:04:29,533 --> 00:04:33,800
(Episode 5)

47
00:04:35,600 --> 00:04:36,900
Morning.

48
00:04:37,300 --> 00:04:38,633
- Morning.
- Morning.

49
00:04:38,733 --> 00:04:40,133
What's going on?

50
00:04:40,467 --> 00:04:42,000
Well...

51
00:04:42,100 --> 00:04:46,067
Serizawa got caught.

52
00:04:46,167 --> 00:04:47,333
Huh? By who?

53
00:04:47,433 --> 00:04:49,100
A senior girl.

54
00:04:49,200 --> 00:04:50,300
Look.

55
00:04:53,200 --> 00:04:54,267
- Not bad.
- No...

56
00:04:54,367 --> 00:04:57,367
I was supposed to play catch
with Takeuchi and the guys.

57
00:04:57,467 --> 00:04:59,600
Then just tell her that.

58
00:05:00,067 --> 00:05:01,733
Did Serizawa do something?

59
00:05:02,367 --> 00:05:03,933
Uh...

60
00:05:04,033 --> 00:05:05,500
Well...

61
00:05:06,933 --> 00:05:08,067
A date?

62
00:05:08,433 --> 00:05:09,133
You know,

63
00:05:09,233 --> 00:05:11,967
remember when we all had that snack party?

64
00:05:12,067 --> 00:05:13,767
Snack party?

65
00:05:15,633 --> 00:05:17,600
I heard Koharu got
them from the senior girls.

66
00:05:17,700 --> 00:05:19,167
Seriously?

67
00:05:19,267 --> 00:05:24,100
Yeah, looks like those offerings
came with strings attached.

68
00:05:24,200 --> 00:05:25,200
Strings attached?

69
00:05:25,267 --> 00:05:27,233
Because he ate those snacks,

70
00:05:27,333 --> 00:05:30,133
Serizawa was asked out on a date.

71
00:05:30,233 --> 00:05:31,300
Huh?

72
00:05:31,400 --> 00:05:33,000
It's not a date.

73
00:05:33,600 --> 00:05:37,067
We're just grabbing
tea together after school.

74
00:05:37,167 --> 00:05:39,267
Just chatting for about an hour.

75
00:05:39,933 --> 00:05:41,967
That's a date.

76
00:05:43,733 --> 00:05:45,733
If you don't want to go, just say no.

77
00:05:45,833 --> 00:05:48,267
I tried to, but...

78
00:05:48,367 --> 00:05:50,067
she was too pushy.

79
00:05:50,733 --> 00:05:52,867
And she said just this once would be fine.

80
00:05:52,967 --> 00:05:54,876
But you don't have to be so
bummed out about it, right?

81
00:05:54,900 --> 00:05:56,300
It's just a date.

82
00:05:56,400 --> 00:06:00,800
You might hit it off and end up dating.

83
00:06:03,500 --> 00:06:06,367
I don't want to deal with
that kind of stuff anymore.

84
00:06:08,067 --> 00:06:13,233
Knowing full well I
can't return her feelings,

85
00:06:13,333 --> 00:06:15,133
I don't want to hurt her for no reason.

86
00:06:19,267 --> 00:06:21,000
The girlfriends Serizawa had in the past,

87
00:06:21,100 --> 00:06:23,567
things always ended up
messy because of that.

88
00:06:30,133 --> 00:06:33,267
Suzuki, you don't think I'm weird, do you?

89
00:06:33,367 --> 00:06:35,300
No, not at all.

90
00:06:35,400 --> 00:06:41,533
It's just... Serizawa, do you...

91
00:06:43,700 --> 00:06:45,367
um...

92
00:06:45,467 --> 00:06:47,433
not have a girlfriend right now?

93
00:06:47,800 --> 00:06:48,833
Yeah.

94
00:06:48,933 --> 00:06:49,833
You're just asking this now?

95
00:06:49,933 --> 00:06:51,433
Ah, sorry.

96
00:06:51,533 --> 00:06:54,300
I just never heard you mention it before.

97
00:06:55,833 --> 00:07:01,300
Nope, I haven't dated
anyone for over a year.

98
00:07:04,767 --> 00:07:08,200
I see. That's pretty surprising.

99
00:07:08,667 --> 00:07:10,627
Except for me, everyone
else is single right now.

100
00:07:10,700 --> 00:07:12,200
Oh, really?

101
00:07:12,300 --> 00:07:13,633
- Yeah.
- Yeah.

102
00:07:13,733 --> 00:07:16,833
I'm good for now.

103
00:07:16,933 --> 00:07:17,933
Just for the record,

104
00:07:18,033 --> 00:07:21,000
I'm strictly in the "no girlfriend" camp.

105
00:07:21,100 --> 00:07:23,233
Iwasaki just wants to play the field.

106
00:07:23,867 --> 00:07:25,276
- That hurt, bumping into me like that.
- I see.

107
00:07:25,300 --> 00:07:26,600
Sorry.

108
00:07:27,933 --> 00:07:29,133
What about you, Suzuki?

109
00:07:30,167 --> 00:07:32,733
Ah, no.

110
00:07:34,033 --> 00:07:36,267
I don't.

111
00:07:36,867 --> 00:07:39,133
I'm not involved in romance at all.

112
00:07:39,800 --> 00:07:41,733
You've never had one, ever?

113
00:07:44,967 --> 00:07:46,233
Yeah.

114
00:07:47,367 --> 00:07:50,133
Hmm... I see.

115
00:07:52,033 --> 00:07:54,833
So when are you going?

116
00:07:54,933 --> 00:07:58,133
On that date with the senior girl.

117
00:07:58,233 --> 00:08:01,067
We haven't decided
yet, and it's not a date.

118
00:08:01,567 --> 00:08:03,543
But if you talk to her,
you might really hit it off.

119
00:08:03,567 --> 00:08:05,900
- A date...
- I told you it's not a date.

120
00:08:06,000 --> 00:08:11,267
- Yes, a date...
- Yes, a date...

121
00:08:12,847 --> 00:08:14,647
A date...
["Date"]

122
00:08:16,333 --> 00:08:17,333
Is it?

123
00:08:19,367 --> 00:08:23,867
If it's Serizawa, I'm sure they'll
have a great time chatting.

124
00:08:26,100 --> 00:08:29,633
And the mood will naturally get romantic.

125
00:08:29,733 --> 00:08:31,833
They'll gradually be drawn to each other.

126
00:08:34,300 --> 00:08:37,467
Maybe they'll even start dating?

127
00:08:43,033 --> 00:08:44,433
Suzuki.

128
00:08:45,733 --> 00:08:47,733
Ah, Serizawa?

129
00:08:48,400 --> 00:08:49,833
I knew you'd be here.

130
00:08:51,100 --> 00:08:52,600
Writing your novel?

131
00:08:53,167 --> 00:08:54,367
Yeah.

132
00:08:59,400 --> 00:09:00,667
Is something wrong?

133
00:09:03,367 --> 00:09:05,167
You seem a bit down.

134
00:09:06,333 --> 00:09:07,533
Something on your mind?

135
00:09:12,033 --> 00:09:13,400
Huh?

136
00:09:14,600 --> 00:09:16,300
A date?

137
00:09:17,800 --> 00:09:19,200
This is...

138
00:09:19,733 --> 00:09:21,500
Are you struggling with

139
00:09:22,233 --> 00:09:24,333
how to write a date scene?

140
00:09:26,967 --> 00:09:29,367
Ah... Yeah, I am.

141
00:09:29,467 --> 00:09:31,767
I don't really know much about dates.

142
00:09:31,867 --> 00:09:32,467
Yeah.

143
00:09:32,567 --> 00:09:34,167
Because I've never been on one.

144
00:09:35,967 --> 00:09:39,533
You should've said so earlier. Just ask me.

145
00:09:40,467 --> 00:09:44,100
Didn't we agree you'd come
to me if you had trouble?

146
00:09:44,967 --> 00:09:46,767
Yeah, thanks.

147
00:09:53,333 --> 00:09:56,800
But I want to try
researching it myself first.

148
00:10:01,833 --> 00:10:03,000
Hmm?

149
00:10:04,300 --> 00:10:06,833
Want to try it out with me?

150
00:10:07,867 --> 00:10:10,067
Huh? Try what?

151
00:10:12,600 --> 00:10:13,900
A date.

152
00:10:22,567 --> 00:10:24,333
I can't believe I actually came.

153
00:10:26,267 --> 00:10:27,500
A date?

154
00:10:27,967 --> 00:10:29,600
Me and Serizawa?

155
00:10:30,367 --> 00:10:32,233
No way...

156
00:10:32,333 --> 00:10:35,300
Do I look weird like this?

157
00:10:35,800 --> 00:10:39,233
I should've at least
bought some new clothes.

158
00:10:39,333 --> 00:10:42,933
Wait, I don't even have clothes nice
enough to wear to go buy clothes.

159
00:10:44,933 --> 00:10:46,300
Suzuki.

160
00:11:01,333 --> 00:11:06,900
H-His casual wear is way too lethal.

161
00:11:09,567 --> 00:11:11,733
Sorry, have you been waiting long?

162
00:11:15,767 --> 00:11:19,700
I knew it... I can't do this.

163
00:11:19,800 --> 00:11:21,233
Where are you going?!

164
00:11:22,733 --> 00:11:28,533
No, it's just that you look
way too handsome, Serizawa.

165
00:11:29,267 --> 00:11:31,000
Come on, I'm flattered.

166
00:11:31,100 --> 00:11:33,260
Besides, I have to dress
up a bit for a date, right?

167
00:11:33,300 --> 00:11:35,267
After all, it's a date with you, Suzuki.

168
00:11:35,700 --> 00:11:36,800
A date...

169
00:11:36,900 --> 00:11:37,800
All right, let's go.

170
00:11:37,900 --> 00:11:39,833
Huh? Where are we going?

171
00:11:39,933 --> 00:11:41,867
Somewhere you'll enjoy.

172
00:11:53,100 --> 00:11:56,333
Isn't this the place from
"Deep Sea and Starry Sky"

173
00:11:56,433 --> 00:11:58,867
where Hasefuka had their first date?

174
00:11:59,733 --> 00:12:01,333
Huh? How did you know?

175
00:12:01,933 --> 00:12:05,033
A date and a pilgrimage all in one.
Kills two birds with one stone, right?

176
00:12:05,900 --> 00:12:07,867
That's Serizawa for you.

177
00:12:08,333 --> 00:12:10,233
This is awesome. I'm so happy!

178
00:12:11,000 --> 00:12:14,000
Ah, I should've brought my acrylic stand.

179
00:12:14,767 --> 00:12:16,900
Here, I knew you'd say that.

180
00:12:18,733 --> 00:12:20,100
It's Hasefuka!

181
00:12:20,300 --> 00:12:22,233
Unbelievable, you're a genius!

182
00:12:22,333 --> 00:12:24,400
You're way too perfect, Serizawa.

183
00:12:24,500 --> 00:12:25,667
Right?

184
00:12:25,767 --> 00:12:27,033
Here.

185
00:12:28,533 --> 00:12:30,167
Hasefuka.

186
00:12:31,533 --> 00:12:32,667
I have to take a picture.

187
00:12:32,767 --> 00:12:34,000
Ah, go ahead.

188
00:12:35,033 --> 00:12:36,400
Okay, I'm taking it.

189
00:12:36,500 --> 00:12:38,267
Come on, say cheese.

190
00:12:42,767 --> 00:12:43,767
Want to take another one?

191
00:12:43,833 --> 00:12:45,267
Let's take one more.

192
00:12:47,100 --> 00:12:49,000
Come on, say cheese.

193
00:12:54,733 --> 00:12:58,233
Wow... There are so many fish.

194
00:12:58,500 --> 00:12:59,867
- You're right.
- Right?

195
00:13:00,400 --> 00:13:02,133
Is that a char?

196
00:13:02,157 --> 00:13:03,497
- A char?
- It's my first time seeing one in person.

197
00:13:08,200 --> 00:13:09,433
Ah!

198
00:13:10,000 --> 00:13:10,667
Right here.

199
00:13:10,767 --> 00:13:12,867
Do you know which scene this is from?

200
00:13:12,967 --> 00:13:14,733
Where Hasefuka held hands?

201
00:13:14,833 --> 00:13:16,033
Yeah.

202
00:13:16,333 --> 00:13:17,733
Here.

203
00:13:18,333 --> 00:13:19,433
Huh?

204
00:13:19,533 --> 00:13:21,033
Aren't we on a date?

205
00:13:21,633 --> 00:13:25,400
B-But this is just for research...

206
00:13:25,500 --> 00:13:26,667
Exactly.

207
00:13:26,767 --> 00:13:30,033
Come on, let's dive deeper
into the dating experience.

208
00:13:36,333 --> 00:13:38,567
No, it should be like this.

209
00:13:42,167 --> 00:13:43,500
Let's go then.

210
00:13:44,400 --> 00:13:45,633
Oh no.

211
00:13:47,333 --> 00:13:48,933
My heart is racing.

212
00:13:49,667 --> 00:13:50,933
So cute!

213
00:13:51,033 --> 00:13:52,233
Wow, there are so many!

214
00:13:52,333 --> 00:13:53,700
What kind of fish are these?

215
00:13:53,800 --> 00:13:54,500
Piranhas.

216
00:13:54,600 --> 00:13:56,133
Definitely not.

217
00:13:57,733 --> 00:13:58,900
So cute!

218
00:13:59,467 --> 00:14:00,467
They're so tiny.

219
00:14:00,667 --> 00:14:02,200
You're right, they're tiny.

220
00:14:02,300 --> 00:14:04,233
Oh, there are even smaller ones.

221
00:14:04,833 --> 00:14:06,633
Is this what I think it is?

222
00:14:06,900 --> 00:14:08,333
Oh, I want to try.

223
00:14:08,433 --> 00:14:11,167
Here, put your hand in.

224
00:14:11,267 --> 00:14:12,467
Huh? Can I really?

225
00:14:12,567 --> 00:14:13,933
Yeah, go ahead.

226
00:14:14,033 --> 00:14:14,900
Here, like this.

227
00:14:15,000 --> 00:14:16,867
Whoa, they're already swarming.

228
00:14:16,967 --> 00:14:19,500
Hey, wait, wait a sec.

229
00:14:19,933 --> 00:14:22,733
Aren't there way too many of them?

230
00:14:23,500 --> 00:14:26,933
Could it be... because of this?

231
00:14:27,033 --> 00:14:28,400
Do you have too much dead skin?

232
00:14:28,500 --> 00:14:30,833
Wait, this is so embarrassing!

233
00:14:31,800 --> 00:14:32,900
Dead skin.

234
00:14:33,000 --> 00:14:34,109
You didn't get bitten, did you?

235
00:14:34,133 --> 00:14:35,267
I'm fine.

236
00:14:46,813 --> 00:14:48,347
A capybara!

237
00:14:48,467 --> 00:14:49,167
Oh.

238
00:14:49,267 --> 00:14:50,967
It poked its head out this time.

239
00:14:51,067 --> 00:14:51,967
It's out.

240
00:14:52,067 --> 00:14:53,633
Just its nose.

241
00:14:53,733 --> 00:14:54,300
So cute.

242
00:14:54,400 --> 00:14:55,600
Oh, there are turtles too.

243
00:14:55,700 --> 00:14:57,100
Ah, you're right, turtles!

244
00:14:57,200 --> 00:14:58,467
So cute.

245
00:15:06,400 --> 00:15:08,133
This is the one Hasefuka shook.

246
00:15:10,467 --> 00:15:12,533
Suzuki, let's do it together.

247
00:15:13,400 --> 00:15:14,400
Okay.

248
00:15:16,667 --> 00:15:18,000
Ready, go.

249
00:15:22,300 --> 00:15:23,300
That startled me.

250
00:15:23,333 --> 00:15:23,867
So many.

251
00:15:23,967 --> 00:15:25,433
I really want to buy one.

252
00:15:25,833 --> 00:15:26,700
I want one too.

253
00:15:26,800 --> 00:15:28,000
Huh?

254
00:15:29,433 --> 00:15:30,767
Oh, so cute.

255
00:15:31,600 --> 00:15:33,433
Let's get matching ones.

256
00:15:35,033 --> 00:15:40,967
Wouldn't that make us
look like a real couple?

257
00:15:44,133 --> 00:15:45,467
Thanks for waiting.

258
00:15:45,567 --> 00:15:47,247
- Thank you.
- Thank you for your purchase.

259
00:15:54,833 --> 00:15:56,967
Hey, isn't that guy super hot?

260
00:15:57,067 --> 00:15:58,733
Yeah, do you think he's a model?

261
00:15:58,833 --> 00:15:59,667
Should we go talk to him?

262
00:15:59,767 --> 00:16:02,567
No way. You'd have to be drop-dead
gorgeous to be in his league.

263
00:16:03,033 --> 00:16:04,553
What do you think his best feature is?

264
00:16:05,133 --> 00:16:07,367
He's handsome and has a great body.

265
00:16:09,400 --> 00:16:10,567
Thanks for waiting.

266
00:16:11,467 --> 00:16:13,333
Blue Hawaii and white soda.

267
00:16:13,433 --> 00:16:14,700
Which one do you want?

268
00:16:15,000 --> 00:16:16,400
Ah, thanks.

269
00:16:17,900 --> 00:16:19,233
Oh, either is fine.

270
00:16:20,933 --> 00:16:22,667
Then this one's yours.

271
00:16:28,067 --> 00:16:29,067
It's good!

272
00:16:29,100 --> 00:16:30,333
Try some of this too.

273
00:16:30,900 --> 00:16:32,567
Ah, okay.

274
00:16:45,233 --> 00:16:47,367
Ah, thanks.

275
00:16:47,467 --> 00:16:48,833
It's pretty good.

276
00:16:51,433 --> 00:16:52,867
What's wrong?

277
00:16:52,967 --> 00:16:54,167
Nothing.

278
00:16:55,533 --> 00:16:58,267
I just feel a bit bad.

279
00:16:58,367 --> 00:16:59,667
Huh?

280
00:17:00,333 --> 00:17:02,400
Someone like me...

281
00:17:02,500 --> 00:17:04,800
Hanging out with you, Serizawa.

282
00:17:06,200 --> 00:17:09,233
Huh? What do you mean by that?

283
00:17:09,333 --> 00:17:10,867
Exactly what it sounds like.

284
00:17:12,333 --> 00:17:18,300
You're handsome and have great style.

285
00:17:19,933 --> 00:17:22,167
Compared to you...

286
00:17:22,267 --> 00:17:27,967
I'm so plain it's embarrassing.

287
00:17:28,767 --> 00:17:31,633
Suzuki, you really lack
confidence, don't you?

288
00:17:32,700 --> 00:17:33,933
Huh?

289
00:17:35,167 --> 00:17:37,633
I couldn't care less
what other people think.

290
00:17:37,733 --> 00:17:39,900
But I absolutely love
you just the way you are.

291
00:17:40,000 --> 00:17:43,200
Like your outfit today, your hair...

292
00:17:43,300 --> 00:17:45,467
Your looks, your
personality, I love it all.

293
00:17:46,100 --> 00:17:49,600
That's... that's a bit of
an exaggeration, isn't it?

294
00:17:49,700 --> 00:17:53,533
And the way you're always so
focused on writing your novel.

295
00:17:53,967 --> 00:17:56,900
Taking notes like this, working so hard...

296
00:17:57,000 --> 00:17:58,400
I love that too.

297
00:17:59,867 --> 00:18:02,533
But my novel...

298
00:18:02,633 --> 00:18:04,600
I haven't even finished a single story yet.

299
00:18:05,600 --> 00:18:08,933
And I only take notes because...

300
00:18:09,033 --> 00:18:11,433
I'm just slower at catching
on than everyone else.

301
00:18:13,867 --> 00:18:18,233
I've never been good
at studying or sports.

302
00:18:19,300 --> 00:18:20,667
No matter what I do...

303
00:18:20,767 --> 00:18:24,767
It takes me way longer than anyone else.

304
00:18:31,100 --> 00:18:32,367
Hey, Suzuki.

305
00:18:33,600 --> 00:18:36,400
Instead of worrying about some random
person's judgment...

306
00:18:36,500 --> 00:18:39,667
I genuinely think you're amazing.

307
00:18:39,767 --> 00:18:41,500
Just trust me on this.

308
00:18:46,233 --> 00:18:48,100
Suzuki, you're adorable.

309
00:18:49,100 --> 00:18:50,867
Out of everyone I want by my side...

310
00:18:50,967 --> 00:18:52,367
You're number one.

311
00:18:58,167 --> 00:18:59,700
Got it?

312
00:19:01,367 --> 00:19:03,267
There, there. Good boy.

313
00:19:03,367 --> 00:19:05,267
Let me go, Serizawa!

314
00:19:07,200 --> 00:19:10,000
No way, no way.

315
00:19:14,867 --> 00:19:16,267
So, how was it?

316
00:19:17,033 --> 00:19:18,600
The date scene.

317
00:19:19,000 --> 00:19:20,400
Think you can write a good one now?

318
00:19:20,933 --> 00:19:23,733
Yeah, thanks to you, Serizawa.

319
00:19:23,833 --> 00:19:25,633
Thank you so much for today.

320
00:19:30,000 --> 00:19:31,400
Huh?

321
00:19:31,933 --> 00:19:35,033
Did you realize where we are?

322
00:19:35,467 --> 00:19:37,733
Is this really where Hasefuka
had their kissing scene?

323
00:19:37,833 --> 00:19:39,367
Yeah, exactly.

324
00:19:42,033 --> 00:19:43,200
That's awesome.

325
00:19:51,600 --> 00:19:53,267
Aren't you going to write it, Suzuki?

326
00:19:53,867 --> 00:19:55,300
A kissing scene.

327
00:19:56,100 --> 00:19:59,567
Yeah, I'm planning to.

328
00:19:59,667 --> 00:20:01,027
At the very end of the date scene.

329
00:20:02,000 --> 00:20:04,900
Oh, how are you going to write it?

330
00:20:06,033 --> 00:20:08,333
Uh...

331
00:20:09,600 --> 00:20:11,033
For example...

332
00:20:11,467 --> 00:20:14,667
The seme doesn't want the
uke to leave, so he stops him.

333
00:20:15,200 --> 00:20:17,067
And asks, "Can I kiss you?"

334
00:20:17,400 --> 00:20:18,733
And then?

335
00:20:20,267 --> 00:20:21,900
That's not bad.

336
00:20:22,467 --> 00:20:26,100
But wouldn't it be better
if it was a bit more natural?

337
00:20:27,700 --> 00:20:28,733
More natural?

338
00:20:32,667 --> 00:20:34,767
Ah, turn around for a sec.

339
00:20:42,133 --> 00:20:46,267
First, their eyes meet by chance.

340
00:20:47,633 --> 00:20:52,467
Then, without saying a word,
they just look at each other.

341
00:20:53,267 --> 00:21:00,933
Next, it slowly feels like their hearts
are melting together.

342
00:21:03,000 --> 00:21:08,867
And before they know it,
it just happens naturally...

343
00:21:37,400 --> 00:21:38,900
How's that?

344
00:21:39,000 --> 00:21:40,433
Get it?

345
00:21:46,933 --> 00:21:48,233
Suzuki?

346
00:21:51,700 --> 00:21:53,100
Oh no.

347
00:21:53,833 --> 00:21:56,900
I... I really can't hold back anymore.

348
00:22:03,467 --> 00:22:04,833
Suzuki?

349
00:22:05,500 --> 00:22:06,833
Look at me.

350
00:22:22,700 --> 00:22:29,267
I really do...

351
00:22:56,667 --> 00:22:57,967
like you, Serizawa.

352
00:23:00,033 --> 00:23:04,233
(Next Episode)
Forget it...

353
00:23:04,700 --> 00:23:05,867
Forget it!

354
00:23:05,967 --> 00:23:06,967
Wh-What?

355
00:23:07,067 --> 00:23:08,067
Nothing.

356
00:23:08,333 --> 00:23:11,333
I just had a really great time yesterday.

357
00:23:11,500 --> 00:23:12,733
Forget it...

358
00:23:12,833 --> 00:23:14,633
How could I possibly forget?
